  "description": "Redevelopment of the site comprising the erection of eight single family dwellings (3 x two storey mews houses to the rear of nos.13-23 Cambridge Grove, 1 x two storey mews house at the northern end of the site adjacent to the railway bridge; and 4 x three storey plus-basement dwelling houses fronting on to Argyle Place); retention of the two storey office building at the southern end of the site (to provide 208 sqm of Class B1 office space) following construction of new roof and side extension, and elevational alterations; provision of 6 no. off street parking spaces; following demolition of all existing timber yard structures on the site and the roof and two storey extension to the office building at the site entrance on Dimes Place.",
